              "output": "[{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"Start by loading the `tidymodels` package...\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"4c6afe7a-2026-4c0f-9330-2d51ece10445\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"library('tidymodels')\",\"execution_count\":1,\"cell_id\":\"e0016e1a-d255-4cb7-9198-b1cb757c65f1\",\"language\":\"R\",\"outputs\":[{\"output_type\":\"stream\",\"text\":\"\u2500\u2500 \\u001b[1mAttaching packages\\u001b[22m \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 tidymodels 1.4.1 \u2500\u2500\\n\\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mbroom       \\u001b[39m 1.0.13     \\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mrecipes     \\u001b[39m 1.4.0 \\n\\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mdials       \\u001b[39m 1.4.4      \\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mrsample     \\u001b[39m 1.3.2 \\n\\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mdplyr       \\u001b[39m 1.2.1      \\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mtailor      \\u001b[39m 0.1.0 \\n\\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mggplot2     \\u001b[39m 4.0.3      \\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mtidyr       \\u001b[39m 1.3.2 \\n\\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34minfer       \\u001b[39m 1.1.0      \\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mtune        \\u001b[39m 2.1.0 \\n\\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mmodeldata   \\u001b[39m 1.6.0      \\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mworkflows   \\u001b[39m 1.3.0 \\n\\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mparsnip     \\u001b[39m 1.6.1      \\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mworkflowsets\\u001b[39m 1.1.1 \\n\\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mpurrr       \\u001b[39m 1.2.2      \\u001b[32m\u2714\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34myardstick   \\u001b[39m 1.4.0 \\n\u2500\u2500 \\u001b[1mConflicts\\u001b[22m \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 tidymodels_conflicts() \u2500\u2500\\n\\u001b[31m\u2716\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mtidyr\\u001b[39m::\\u001b[32mcomplete()\\u001b[39m masks \\u001b[34mhera\\u001b[39m::complete()\\n\\u001b[31m\u2716\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mpurrr\\u001b[39m::\\u001b[32mdiscard()\\u001b[39m  masks \\u001b[34mscales\\u001b[39m::discard()\\n\\u001b[31m\u2716\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mdplyr\\u001b[39m::\\u001b[32mfilter()\\u001b[39m   masks \\u001b[34mstats\\u001b[39m::filter()\\n\\u001b[31m\u2716\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mdplyr\\u001b[39m::\\u001b[32mlag()\\u001b[39m      masks \\u001b[34mstats\\u001b[39m::lag()\\n\\u001b[31m\u2716\\u001b[39m \\u001b[34mrecipes\\u001b[39m::\\u001b[32mstep()\\u001b[39m   masks \\u001b[34mstats\\u001b[39m::step()\\n\\u001b[34m\u2022\\u001b[39m Learn how to get started at \\u001b[32mhttps://www.tidymodels.org/start/\\u001b[39m\\n\"}]},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"Let's work with [hotel bookings data](https://github.com/rfordatascience/tidytuesday/blob/master/data/2020/2020-02-11/readme.md) from TidyTuesday. \",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"c19dd902-7659-4915-91f9-6591ea87537f\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"hotels = \\n  readr::read_csv(\\\"https://tidymodels.org/start/case-study/hotels.csv\\\", col_types = readr::cols()) |>\\n  mutate(across(where(is.character), as.factor)) # turns all categorical columns into factors\\n\\nhotels |> head()\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"a3440bf4-e884-4c37-80bd-bd54ca3c6a05\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"Each row is a \\\"stay\\\" and we want to predict whether the stay included children given the other features.\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"f06360e4-3193-4b3e-a5ea-8b10114a788e\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"We'll want to extract a bit more information from the `arrival_date` column. So, let's make a `recipe`.\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"c42fc696-78f2-4566-b6d7-d5aa63224894\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"rec = recipe(children ~ ., data = hotels) |>\\n    step_date(arrival_date) |>\\n    step_holiday(arrival_date) |>\\n    step_rm(arrival_date) |>\\n    prep()\",\"execution_count\":3,\"cell_id\":\"57bbe244-26a5-457d-a590-5c9c3b73a881\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"What does this recipe do? Look at the transformed data with \\\"juice\\\".\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"786a3e66-ca41-4d47-bf8b-5960b5110355\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"rec |> juice() |> head()\",\"execution_count\":4,\"cell_id\":\"f2dc7e10-74a1-4268-a60e-13abcb4dd55f\",\"language\":\"R\",\"outputs\":[{\"output_type\":\"execute_result\",\"text\":\"  hotel        lead_time stays_in_weekend_nights stays_in_week_nights adults\\n1 City_Hotel   217       1                       3                    2     \\n2 City_Hotel     2       0                       1                    2     \\n3 Resort_Hotel  95       2                       5                    2     \\n4 Resort_Hotel 143       2                       6                    2     \\n5 Resort_Hotel 136       1                       4                    2     \\n6 City_Hotel    67       2                       2                    2     \\n  meal country market_segment distribution_channel is_repeated_guest \u22ef\\n1 BB   DEU     Offline_TA/TO  TA/TO                0                 \u22ef\\n2 BB   PRT     Direct         Direct               0                 \u22ef\\n3 BB   GBR     Online_TA      TA/TO                0                 \u22ef\\n4 HB   ROU     Online_TA      TA/TO                0                 \u22ef\\n5 HB   PRT     Direct         Direct               0                 \u22ef\\n6 SC   GBR     Online_TA      TA/TO                0                 \u22ef\\n  average_daily_rate required_car_parking_spaces total_of_special_requests\\n1  80.75             none                        1                        \\n2 170.00             none                        3                        \\n3   8.00             none                        2                        \\n4  81.00             none                        1                        \\n5 157.60             none                        4                        \\n6  49.09             none                        1                        \\n  children arrival_date_dow arrival_date_month arrival_date_year\\n1 none     Thu              Sep                2016             \\n2 none     Fri              Aug                2017             \\n3 none     Sat              Nov                2016             \\n4 none     Tue              Apr                2016             \\n5 none     Wed              Dec                2016             \\n6 none     Sun              Mar                2016             \\n  arrival_date_LaborDay arrival_date_NewYearsDay arrival_date_ChristmasDay\\n1 0                     0                        0                        \\n2 0                     0                        0                        \\n3 0                     0                        0                        \\n4 0                     0                        0                        \\n5 0                     0                        0                        \\n6 0                     0                        0                        \",\"image\":null}]},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"Let's start with a decision tree. \",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"3e33bfac-521c-4af6-8bea-5349f6c2546d\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"mod = decision_tree() |>\\n    set_engine('rpart') |>\\n    set_mode('classification')\",\"execution_count\":5,\"cell_id\":\"704b51a9-e57c-445f-8569-15fff2d70c0a\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"Fit `mod` using the data from your prepped recipe. (Hint: remember `juice`).\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"da6b48d4-3f11-4dab-86fb-189a04e6845d\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"mod_fit = mod |> fit(children ~ ., data = juice(rec))\",\"execution_count\":6,\"cell_id\":\"850b6234-951b-46ff-99d8-0c8576918db4\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"Use the snippet below to visualize the tree. What is the first split?\\n\\n```r\\nrpart.plot::rpart.plot(mod_fit$fit)\\n```\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"e2b8f7b5-a3a8-4099-b2b0-29771c8811b9\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"rpart.plot::rpart.plot(mod_fit$fit)\",\"execution_count\":7,\"cell_id\":\"b90247ac-ece1-4626-bb09-13901717dde9\",\"language\":\"R\",\"outputs\":[{\"output_type\":\"stream\",\"text\":\"Outputs are too large to include. Use command with: cat <notebook_path> | jq '.cells[14].outputs'\"}]},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"Now create a `random_forest` model and fit it to the transformed `hotels` data.\\n\\n1. the `mode` should be \\\"classification\\\", and,\\n2. add `importance = \\\"impurity\\\"` to `set_engine` so we can calculate feature importances with the model.\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"02d0ad38-a48e-4a62-a792-e2b1099477bf\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"rf_mod = rand_forest() |>\\n    set_engine('ranger', importance = 'impurity') |>\\n    set_mode('classification')\\n\\nrf_fit = rf_mod |> fit(children ~ ., data = juice(rec))\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"d680e3f3-a698-459c-94c3-f5ec50e494c9\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"We can plot the feature importances. Pipe your fitted model into `extract_fit_engine()` and then into `vip(num_features = 20)`.\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"c92b4371-2c51-4124-8e8f-29f1a4decde4\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"rf_fit |> extract_fit_engine() |> vip(num_features = 20)\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"4fa1f375-66db-4e59-8ec6-78b8cb39b4f7\",\"language\":\"R\"}]"
            },
